KNOWNBUG
partial-assignment-before-non-constant-index1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.v\[7:4\] == 4'b1111\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The assignment to v[i] is rewritten into an assignment to the whole of
v, using the value of v before the assignment. That value is taken to
be the current-state value of v whenever no single recorded slice
covers all of v, and hence the preceding blocking assignment to
v[7:4] is lost.
